# Committed render snapshots are compared byte for byte (tests/test_vrt.py), so the bytes
# in the working tree must be the bytes that were captured.  Git on Windows rewrites LF
# to CRLF on checkout by default, which would fail every snapshot on four of the twelve
# CI legs; `eol=lf` pins the checkout on every platform.  The test normalises line endings
# on read as well, so a checkout that ignores this file still passes -- belt and braces,
# because a snapshot that is red for a reason unrelated to rendering teaches people to
# rebaseline without looking.
tests/vrt/**/*.svg text eol=lf
